  "scenario": "r1 has two ports wired together and a diagnostic loopback 192.0.2.1/32 on lo0.0. An aggregate 172.17.0.0/16 is already defined as passive and is active in the ordinary route view. Build a service endpoint, two planned static routes, and aggregates where only the approved contributor is accepted.",
  "schemaVersion": 0,
  "stages": [
    {
      "checks": [
        {
          "command": "show interfaces ge-0/0/0.0 terse",
          "container": "interface-information",
          "description": "ge-0/0/0.0 carries 192.0.2.2/24",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s1-if",
          "records": "interface-address",
          "type": "state-match",
          "where": {
            "ifa-local": "192.0.2.2/24"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "Direct route 192.0.2.0/24",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s1-rt",
          "prefix": "192.0.2.0/24",
          "protocol": "Direct",
          "table": "inet.0",
          "type": "route-exists"
        },
        {
          "count": 3,
          "description": "r1 pings 192.0.2.2",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s1-ping",
          "min_success_rate": 1,
          "target": "192.0.2.2",
          "type": "ping"
        }
      ],
      "commonMistakes": [
        {
          "mistake": "Using /32 or the wrong port",
          "recognise": "The address shows on ge-0/0/1.0 or with /32 in the interface readback",
          "symptom": "No Direct 192.0.2.0/24 route"
        }
      ],
      "doneWhen": [
        "Operational state shows 192.0.2.2/24 on ge-0/0/0.0.",
        "inet.0 has an active Direct route 192.0.2.0/24.",
        "r1 pings 192.0.2.2."
      ],
      "explanation": [
        "The interface readback shows the address and mask on the named unit.",
        "The Direct route is derived from that mask and the ping then succeeds locally."
      ],
      "goal": "Give r1 a service endpoint on its first wired port so that the local subnet is connected and reachable.",
      "hint": "Check the interface readback for the unit, address and mask.",
      "id": "s1",
      "solution": {
        "r1": [
          "set interfaces ge-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 192.0.2.2/24"
        ]
      },
      "title": "Establish the exact local service endpoint"
    },
    {
      "checks": [
        {
          "command": "show route 172.16.10.0/24 exact",
          "container": "route-information",
          "description": "172.16.10.0/24 active static discard",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s2-d-rt",
          "records": "rt-entry",
          "type": "state-match",
          "where": {
            "active-tag": "*",
            "nh-type": "Discard",
            "protocol-name": "Static"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "show route 172.17.10.0/24 exact",
          "container": "route-information",
          "description": "172.17.10.0/24 active static reject",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s2-r-rt",
          "records": "rt-entry",
          "type": "state-match",
          "where": {
            "active-tag": "*",
            "nh-type": "Reject",
            "protocol-name": "Static"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "discard forwarding entry",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s2-d-fw",
          "next_hop_type": "dscd",
          "prefix": "172.16.10.0/24",
          "type": "forwarding-table-entry"
        },
        {
          "description": "reject forwarding entry",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s2-r-fw",
          "next_hop_type": "rjct",
          "prefix": "172.17.10.0/24",
          "type": "forwarding-table-entry"
        }
      ],
      "commonMistakes": [
        {
          "mistake": "Swapping discard and reject",
          "recognise": "dscd appears where rjct is expected or the reverse",
          "symptom": "Forwarding entry type is swapped"
        }
      ],
      "doneWhen": [
        "172.16.10.0/24 is active Static with a discard next hop and a discard forwarding entry.",
        "172.17.10.0/24 is active Static with a reject next hop and a reject forwarding entry."
      ],
      "explanation": [
        "Discard drops silently; reject drops and returns an unreachable.",
        "The route view and forwarding table show Discard/dscd and Reject/rjct."
      ],
      "goal": "Create the two planned networks as local static routes that drop traffic in two different ways.",
      "hint": "One drops silently, the other signals unreachable.",
      "id": "s2",
      "solution": {
        "r1": [
          "set routing-options static route 172.16.10.0/24 discard",
          "set routing-options static route 172.17.10.0/24 reject"
        ]
      },
      "title": "Represent the two planned networks"
    },
    {
      "checks": [
        {
          "command": "show route 172.16.0.0/16 exact",
          "container": "route-information",
          "description": "172.16.0.0/16 active Aggregate",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s3-agg",
          "records": "rt-entry",
          "type": "state-match",
          "where": {
            "active-tag": "*",
            "protocol-name": "Aggregate"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "show route hidden 172.17.0.0/16 exact",
          "container": "route-information",
          "description": "172.17.0.0/16 Aggregate retained in hidden view",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s3-hid",
          "records": "rt-entry",
          "type": "state-match",
          "where": {
            "protocol-name": "Aggregate"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "show route 172.17.0.0/16 exact",
          "container": "route-information",
          "description": "172.17.0.0/16 absent from the ordinary view",
          "device": "r1",
          "id": "s3-ord",
          "negate": true,
          "records": "rt-entry",
          "type": "state-match",
          "where": {
            "protocol-name": "Aggregate"
          }
        }
      ],
      "commonMistakes": [
        {
          "mistake": "Leaving the passive setting on 172.17.0.0/16",
          "recognise": "show route 172.17.0.0/16 exact still lists the Aggregate",
          "symptom": "172.17.0.0/16 stays active in the ordinary view"
        }
      ],
      "doneWhen": [
        "172.16.0.0/16 is an active Aggregate.",
        "172.17.0.0/16 appears as Aggregate in the hidden view only, not in the ordinary view."
      ],
      "explanation": [
        "The aggregate policy accepts only the exact approved contributor and rejects the rest.",
        "With no accepted contributor, and the passive setting removed, 172.17.0.0/16 stays in the hidden view, so it is excluded by policy, not deleted."
      ],
      "goal": "Use policy so only the 172.16.10.0/24 contributor builds an aggregate 172.16.0.0/16; the 172.17.0.0/16 aggregate must stay defined but be inactive and hidden.",
      "hint": "An aggregate with no accepted contributor is kept hidden; the passive setting keeps it active regardless.",
      "id": "s3",
      "solution": {
        "r1": [
          "delete routing-options aggregate route 172.17.0.0/16 passive",
          "set policy-options policy-statement AGG-CONTRIB term approved from route-filter 172.16.10.0/24 exact",
          "set policy-options policy-statement AGG-CONTRIB term approved then accept",
          "set policy-options policy-statement AGG-CONTRIB term rest then reject",
          "set routing-options aggregate route 172.16.0.0/16 policy AGG-CONTRIB",
          "set routing-options aggregate route 172.17.0.0/16 policy AGG-CONTRIB"
        ]
      },
      "title": "Distinguish rejected contribution from route deletion"
    }
  ],
  "startState": {
    "configs": {
      "r1": [
        "set system host-name r1",
        "set interfaces lo0 unit 0 family inet address 192.0.2.1/32",
        "set routing-options aggregate route 172.17.0.0/16 passive"
      ]
    },
    "description": "r1 has ge-0/0/0 and ge-0/0/1 up/up, joined by a self-link, and lo0.0 holds 192.0.2.1/32. Aggregate 172.17.0.0/16 is defined as passive and is active in the ordinary route view. Nothing else is configured."
  },
  "summary": "Add a service address, two static routes and aggregate contributor policy on one router.",
  "title": "Interface Addressing, Static Routes, and Contributor Policy",
